{
  "Comment": "Table-share control plane (SPEC-088 skeleton; verbs real since SPEC-089→092). validate-authorize → inspect-source run once per request; a Map fans out over $.recipients running check-target-absent → copy-objects → create-table per recipient with a per-item Catch (one recipient's failure never aborts its siblings — architecture §2). ShapeSummary/RecordFailure carry the structured terminal outcomes SPEC-094 notifies from. Each Task threads the running object via Payload.$=$ + OutputPath=$.Payload; only transient Lambda SERVICE errors are retried.",
  "StartAt": "ValidateAuthorize",
  "States": {
    "ValidateAuthorize": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Comment": "First step (real since SPEC-089): verifies the ID token into the actor, authorizes source access, validates the result name, annotates recipients. The Pipe forwards the raw SQS batch (a JSON ARRAY), so Payload.$=$ hands the array to the validator (it reads record[0]); OutputPath=$.Payload makes the validated request object the whole state for the next steps. A failure here runs BEFORE the request identity exists, so its Catch (no ResultPath — the input is an array, not an object) routes to ValidateFailureSeed, which seeds null identity fields so the shared recorded-failure state can reference them uniformly. TransientError (a throttled Cognito/S3 read) is retried, never terminalized.",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${validate_authorize_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "Next": "ValidateFailureSeed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "InspectSource"
    },
    "InspectSource": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${inspect_source_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "RecordFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ShareToRecipients"
    },
    "ShareToRecipients": {
      "Type": "Map",
      "Comment": "Per-recipient fan-out (architecture §2). Each item runs the three recipient verbs in sequence; the per-item Catch records that recipient failed WITHOUT aborting siblings. ItemSelector hands each iteration its recipient plus the full request context; the per-recipient results collect under $.recipientResults.",
      "ItemsPath": "$.recipients",
      "MaxConcurrency": 5,
      "ItemSelector": {
        "recipient.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value",
        "request.$": "$"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.recipientResults",
      "ItemProcessor": {
        "ProcessorConfig": {
          "Mode": "INLINE"
        },
        "StartAt": "CheckTargetAbsent",
        "States": {
          "CheckTargetAbsent": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${check_target_absent_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "CopyObjects"
          },
          "CopyObjects": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${copy_objects_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "CreateTable"
          },
          "CreateTable": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${create_table_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "Catch": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
                "ResultPath": "$.error",
                "Next": "RecipientFailed"
              }
            ],
            "Next": "RecipientSucceeded"
          },
          "RecipientSucceeded": {
            "Type": "Pass",
            "Comment": "Per-recipient success record (SPEC-092 final shape): a flat {kind, name, status} summary entry — what ShapeSummary collects and SPEC-094 notifications read.",
            "Parameters": {
              "kind.$": "$.recipient.kind",
              "name.$": "$.recipient.name",
              "status": "ok"
            },
            "End": true
          },
          "RecipientFailed": {
            "Type": "Pass",
            "Comment": "Per-item terminal-failure record (flat summary entry). Ends the ITEM, not the Map: sibling recipients continue. `error` carries the raw {Error, Cause}; the verb's reason (unknown_user/unknown_space/conflict/target_not_readable/copy_failed/create_failed…) is recovered from it with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason. `error` is the RAW Step Functions {Error, Cause}; decode it in Python with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason, NEVER in ASL (States.StringToJson raises an uncatchable States.Runtime on any Cause that is absent or not JSON).",
            "Parameters": {
              "kind.$": "$.recipient.kind",
              "name.$": "$.recipient.name",
              "status": "failed",
              "error.$": "$.error"
            },
            "End": true
          }
        }
      },
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "RecordFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ShapeSummary"
    },
    "ShapeSummary": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "The whole-request success outcome (SPEC-092 FR-003): identity + the per-recipient summary array collected from the Map ({kind, name, status:'ok'|'failed', error?} each — `error` is the RAW Step Functions {Error, Cause}; decode it with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason, never in ASL). The Succeed state passes this through as the execution output — what SPEC-094's sender/recipient notifications read.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "source.$": "$.source",
        "tableName.$": "$.tableName",
        "results.$": "$.recipientResults"
      },
      "Next": "Succeeded"
    },
    "ValidateFailureSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "A validate-authorize failure occurs before the request identity exists (its input was the raw SQS array), so its Catch replaced the state with the error object. Seed null identity fields + carry the error under $.error so the shared RecordFailure path is uniform for every whole-request failure.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor": null,
        "source": { "database": null, "table": null },
        "tableName": null,
        "error.$": "$"
      },
      "Next": "RecordFailure"
    },
    "RecordFailure": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "The single recorded-failure state every whole-request Catch reaches (identity is null for a pre-identity validate failure). Shapes the structured outcome { actor, source, tableName, status:'failed', error } SPEC-094 notifies from, then fails the execution. It carries the RAW $.error {Error, Cause}, not a decoded reason: the ParseError Pass state that used to produce one ran States.StringToJson, which raises an UNCATCHABLE States.Runtime whenever Cause is absent or is not JSON (States.Timeout, States.DataLimitExceeded, Lambda.Unknown — verified live), killing the execution before it could record anything. Decode with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason, never in ASL. Per-RECIPIENT failures never come here — they end their Map item via RecipientFailed and siblings continue.",
      "Parameters": {
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "source.$": "$.source",
        "tableName.$": "$.tableName",
        "status": "failed",
        "error.$": "$.error"
      },
      "Next": "NotifyFailure"
    },
    "NotifyFailure": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Comment": "SPEC-152 FR-001. Emit the friendly failure notification for the failures NO VERB CAN CATCH — a cold-start import error, a state timeout, a task that could not be invoked — where @notifies_on_failure never ran and the sender would otherwise be told nothing at all. WHOLE-REQUEST ONLY, and that needs no guard: a per-recipient failure ends its Map ITEM at RecipientFailed and the execution SUCCEEDS, so it never reaches RecordFailure and cannot arrive here. The duplicate this DOES have to avoid is the whole-request verb's own decorator emit, which the verb suppresses in Python by reading Lambda's Error name. Its Catch goes straight to Failed: a missed notification must never change the recorded outcome, and the execution has already failed.",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${notify_failure_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.notified",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.notifyError",
          "Next": "Failed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Failed"
    },
    "Succeeded": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    },
    "Failed": {
      "Type": "Fail",
      "Error": "TableShareFailed",
      "Cause": "The table-share control plane recorded an unrecoverable whole-request error (see the RecordFailure state output for the structured { status:'failed', reason } outcome)."
    }
  }
}
